# Same meaning as wsa_systemapp.cil, but as .te — the only format that
# SYSTEM_EXT_PRIVATE_SEPOLICY_DIRS accepts at build time. Needed for two reasons
# (22.09.2026, second aosp_wsa_x86_64 build): without at least one .te in the directory
# system/sepolicy/Android.mk does not set HAS_SYSTEM_EXT_SEPOLICY and does not put
# system_ext_sepolicy.cil into the image at all (on LineageOS a .te comes from vendor/lineage/sepolicy) — and then
# bin/transplant-a14.sh has nothing to append wsa_vendor_compat.cil to; also the SystemApp service
# ends up in the policy natively, without a post-patch. wsa_vendor_compat.cil (version-compat of Microsoft
# vendor types, typeattributeset) cannot be expressed in .te and is still appended by transplant.
type wsa_systemapp_service, service_manager_type;
allow priv_app wsa_systemapp_service:service_manager find;
allow system_app wsa_systemapp_service:service_manager add;
allow system_server wsa_systemapp_service:service_manager find;

# The IWsaNotifications service that SystemApp registers last during initialization (on Microsoft's image
# SystemUIApp looks it up). Without the type addService gets "SELinux denied", the exception aborts
# SystemApp initialization, and then waitForNetworkReady/notifyInitialized are never run, while
# the geocoder's waitForInitialized and the Lifetime channel heartbeat hang forever (host logcat, 27.09.2026).
type wsa_notification_service, service_manager_type;
allow priv_app wsa_notification_service:service_manager find;
allow system_app wsa_notification_service:service_manager add;
